# Optional custom firmware features - the single source of truth for the DEFAULT build.
#
# One -D definition per feature. A definition listed in CUSTOM_DEFINES below is compiled into every
# firmware target (Original Tracker, Tracker+, Tracker Mini) and into the GitHub Actions builds. A feature
# that is not listed is compiled out and the firmware behaves like stock Tracker CE for that feature.
#
#   To enable a feature:   add its -D line to CUSTOM_DEFINES.
#   To disable a feature:  remove its -D line (or comment it out).
#   After ANY change here (or to a command-line override) run `make clean` before building: the makefiles do
#   not track compiler flags, so stale object files would give an inconsistent feature mix.
#
# Command-line overrides replace this whole list for one build and do not edit this file, e.g.
#   make clean && make plus CUSTOM_DEFINES="-DMOD_PATTERN_SETTINGS"
#   make clean && make plus CUSTOM_DEFINES=""
#
# Completed and accepted custom features are enabled in the default build. Keep a feature out only
# for a documented reason (for example, experimental status, compatibility, or resource constraints).
# Documentation: docs/custom-firmware/README.md

CUSTOM_DEFINES ?= \
    -DMOD_PATTERN_BPM \
    -DMOD_PATTERN_SETTINGS \
    -DMOD_SAMPLE_BOUNDARY_CAPTURE \
    -DMOD_LAZY_CHOP \
    -DMOD_SHIFT_PATTERN_QUANTIZE
